  "title": "Coffee Lectures Das Neue Programm Ist Da",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "How it works",
      "text": "- New options for open-access publications in 2023 – 8 February 2023\n\n- swisscovery: a brief guide to ordering documents – 15 February 2023\n\n- Get to know the Data Stewardship Network – 22 February 2023\n\n- Research in Dimensions – 1 March 2023\n\n- Compressed Knowledge – Insights into the getAbstract database – 8 March 2023\n\nAt our events, you can find out about your open-access publishing options, take a crash course in the new swisscovery ordering system, or learn about the Data Stewardship Network. The new events programme is now online."
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works",
      "text": "Each session lasts 15 minutes. You will receive concise, condensed information on a particular topic and have time to ask questions at the end. Just the right length of time to enjoy a coffee while you listen and get to know the people behind the ETH Library.\n\nThe online events are held via Zoom at 3.15 p.m. on Wednesday afternoons from 8 February to 8 March 2023. We host the events in English.\n\nYou can take part without registering. For browser-based Zoom sessions, we recommend using Chrome."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Always up to date",
      "text": "Good to know: if you miss an event, you can still access it. We record the sessions and provide access to the presentation slides.\n\nAre you interested in a particular topic? Then we look forward to receiving your suggestion. Whether you have questions regarding a certain tool or want information on a topic relating to information searches, academic writing or publishing – send us your suggested topic at and we will see whether it is suitable for this event series.\n\nMore than just data – Benefit from know-how\n\n#KnowHow – The ETH Library’s infrastructure and tools lead you to your goal."
    }
  ],
